INSERT INTO Review VALUES('21ee790c-ef51-48b8-8441-7dc95c597cbd','dfc915e8-b7c2-4b7c-94ab-59c926396e5f',replace('It was a nice visit. They had sink and washrooms. Alpacas in front. They offered free tea samples. Some shade inside.\n\nIt was a stop during one of the tours. Cool to see the traditional clothing.','\n',char(10)),'Vu Dang',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('1d31990a-057c-4eed-b011-6cc587cd2534','dfc915e8-b7c2-4b7c-94ab-59c926396e5f','Excelente para hacer compras','Isabel Auccapuma',4);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('7661ed33-45d6-444c-9e9f-ac19fe9113e5','0d1777fc-c222-4dd6-bd75-9fb8703817d0','Está bonita la tienda !, la tienda y la explicación de los procesos y te puedes sacar con fotos con alpacas  ; el único detalle que si es más caro  gorros de baby alpaca en 120 ; más bien como vente tratan si le pides a menos le bajan  :( pero la tienda está bonita .. si vas a comprar tejidos. Recomiendo el mercado de pisac','sandra niccals',3);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('08141bda-8994-4c2a-8811-6a8ff29791ce','0d1777fc-c222-4dd6-bd75-9fb8703817d0','Uno de las mejores paradas que hice en el tour. Las mujeres artesanas explicaron muy bien el proceso de extracción de los tintes naturales y la diferencia entre una prenda de baby alpaca y una sintética.','Laura Ortiz C.',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('74e2a165-9a74-4d42-91ad-6fcc89dfb0b8','0d1777fc-c222-4dd6-bd75-9fb8703817d0','Hermoso. Tienen una excelente explicación que entretiene.','Yudy Carpio Monge',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('e4602627-2b02-472d-9e06-cd328cbaa947','936e2c48-2df1-4ab1-bd51-a15675a7dee1',replace('Durante nuestra visita a Chinchero, incluimos una experiencia exclusiva en el centro textil Manos Andinas, una propuesta de cultura viva cuidadosamente seleccionada por su autenticidad y calidad, muy por encima de las textilerías convencionales de la zona.\n\nA diferencia de los espacios tradicionales, aquí el viajero se conecta realmente con el legado andino, participando de una experiencia interpretativa donde artesanas locales comparten, de manera cercana y genuina, las técnicas ancestrales del tejido, los procesos naturales de teñido y el profundo significado cultural de cada diseño.\n\nEl entorno eleva aún más la experiencia: desde este privilegiado punto se aprecia una vista panorámica excepcional hacia la Laguna Piuray, creando un escenario perfecto para disfrutar con calma y tomar fotografías memorables.\n\nComo valor añadido, el lugar cuenta con un espacio especialmente acondicionado para picnic, ideal para quienes buscan una pausa diferente, en contacto con la naturaleza y lejos de los circuitos masivos.\n\nUna experiencia pensada para viajeros que buscan autenticidad, tranquilidad y una conexión real con la cultura andina.','\n',char(10)),'Mateo Lovon Pumasupa',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('2b6e66d7-20f7-44d3-8aa8-361e6b87dc56','936e2c48-2df1-4ab1-bd51-a15675a7dee1','Me encantó Un lugar realmente hermoso ✨ La experiencia fue increíble y la atención de primera.','Lizbeth Quispe ttito',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('dd3b71e2-65b7-4aa9-9a5e-a67152d2147d','936e2c48-2df1-4ab1-bd51-a15675a7dee1','Brindan Excelente servicio y muy bien recomendable para visitar en tu visita a Chinchero. Centro textil chinchero','Paulina TTito Aucapuma',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('d813af40-5fee-4d40-98fa-1bbe4b89337b','f0ce0bd0-48d5-433e-b448-ab863dcc55bb','Really nice place with good quality authentic Peruvian textiles.  Super friendly staff.','Delilah Taylor',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('35686043-17a2-4cdd-89b9-ac32527cc0fa','f0ce0bd0-48d5-433e-b448-ab863dcc55bb','Belleza','Mercy Diaz Alfaro',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('e13dc08c-c38e-41b3-b18b-96574fe51f1f','b8fdaf41-d95a-47c8-adc3-211c09d91a38','J''ai appris la teinture naturel et j''ai tissé un jolie bracelet avec Norberta qui est d''une gentillesse incroyable ! On a déjeuné avec son mari Alfredo, c''était délicieux ! Allez y les yeux fermés !!','Julien-yacine CHAQRA',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('5743c93d-0a2d-48dc-8dad-65d60956e6ed','95eda889-098f-4b48-bac4-2a8a4ceb184c','Personally, it is the best textile center in the area. It has a privileged view, its own parking, the people are very friendly, and they offer a very beautiful dance experience. I highly recommend 📍Balcón del Inka🇵🇪','Swanhild Fanola',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('062e94ae-25dc-4c99-8e48-fba7f334359f','95eda889-098f-4b48-bac4-2a8a4ceb184c','Great presentation. I love places like this show how they create the colors and material. I love to buy things here and try to support as many families as possible. They table with goods made from different families.','JIM INOKUCHI',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('c6652fd3-5f02-458e-a16e-e2826356dd54','95eda889-098f-4b48-bac4-2a8a4ceb184c','Had a nice time learning about how wools are traditionally dyed and spun here. Prices might be more expensive than elsewhere in Peru, but not bad by UK standards. Lovely people!','Charlotte',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('be9b3dc5-9b07-4204-b9c7-66be3409d3f7','92be90ae-7c44-4ba6-a24c-537f63a798b1','Willka T''ika is an incredible place!  I can''t speak highly enough of the accommodations, the grounds, the cultural experiences offered, the food, and most importantly, the warm and welcoming staff who make Willka T''ika the phenomenal place it is!  I dearly hope I am able to return one day. 🙏🏼','Kathee Hansen',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('69ea7ab8-f7fb-41fd-8bf2-2ba9c0082c69','92be90ae-7c44-4ba6-a24c-537f63a798b1','This is the ultimate experience for a retreat. You will be held within the arms of such beautiful people and inspiring gardens. Not to mention the yoga studios, sound room, meditation space and library. It is an experience like no other.','Kim Kent',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('bb0ff88e-9b7b-4f6a-b62a-587830a1761b','92be90ae-7c44-4ba6-a24c-537f63a798b1','The most phenomenal experience I’ve ever had couldn’t fault it in anyway','jacquie saunders',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('50476b02-1f86-40a3-8439-ab223220a99a','33cc3e74-efb9-47e9-a09f-caad723448ba',replace('I find it difficult to put into words what I just experienced after one week on retreat with Master Healers Alan and Dianna Waugh.\n\nTheir mastery of ancient techniques is something I have only read about but never found.\n\nOnly when the harmonic frequencies are aligned will you be called to experience their holy work.\n\nI know in my heart it was by Divine design that I made it to Sacred Valley Spiritual Retreat when I did. We’re in the era of ascension—if you feel the call, answer it.','\n',char(10)),'C Z',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('41231bcd-5f8e-44d6-a11d-2b8782bcdc39','33cc3e74-efb9-47e9-a09f-caad723448ba','It was a magical time for my first visit to Mount Shasta. I had reached out to Alan and Dianna about visiting them in Ecuador. By serendipity, we learned that we were all in California at the time and decided to meet in Mount Shasta for a weekend of personal healing and reflection. From the very beginning of our interactions, I sensed a welcoming and kind nature from Alan and Dianna. They helped create a personal itinerary for me. We did different forms of healing, including: reiki, hypnosis, meditation, and shamanic work. Each experience was unique and very helpful. We also spent time on the Mountain and also visited beautiful waterfalls. By luck, it was also lion''s gate portal and a full moon. I thoroughly enjoyed my time in Shasta and highly recommend Alan and Dianna for their healing work. They both made me feel safe and welcomed and have helped me tremendously.','Rania Karkar',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('c8d354f4-fb17-4b0a-bfae-c1d906890507','33cc3e74-efb9-47e9-a09f-caad723448ba',replace('Before I even arrived, I felt held. As a petite woman traveling solo, I had initial hesitations about journeying to Ecuador—but Alan and Dianna made every step feel effortless. From airport pickups to local transitions, their care and clarity dissolved my fears. I felt safe, supported, and gently guided from the moment I said yes.\n\nI’ll admit, I was obsessed. I kept circling back to their website, drawn to something I couldn’t quite name—Alan’s presence, Dianna’s warmth, the valley itself. It felt like a soul-level invitation. After meeting them over Zoom, I knew. There was no pressure, no persuasion—just a loving suggestion to read Alan’s book and see if it resonated. It did. Deeply. I even left a review on Audible. Within days, I secured my space.\n\nWhat struck me most was how personalized everything was. There was no rigid schedule or group format. The retreat was shaped entirely around me—my timing, my needs, my healing. I was welcomed into a spacious, private guest house with every amenity I could need. I had room to breathe, reflect, and integrate, yet Alan and Dianna were just steps away whenever I needed support.\n\nThe experience itself? Beyond words. The Ayahuasca ceremonies were profound, but what truly set this apart were the co-modalities they offered—breathwork, energy healing, trauma release, and more. It was a full-spectrum journey designed to help me shed layers of density and open fully to the medicine.\n\nAlan and Dianna held me with such compassion and presence. I felt safe, seen, and deeply supported—not just during the retreat, but afterward too. Their integration support continued once I returned home, helping me anchor the transformation into my daily life.\n\nI can’t imagine experiencing Ayahuasca for the first time in any other format. This wasn’t just a retreat—it was a homecoming. I feel whole. I feel peace. I feel love.\n\nI’m eternally grateful to Alan and Dianna. This may just become my annual pilgrimage.','\n',char(10)),'artizen matrix',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('0a65ad07-904a-45f5-8ac3-21a36705959b','a3cbc4d7-ad40-4340-a1eb-1deff4d2c93f','The best place for a retreat','Elsa Maria Zaplana vargas',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('3695618d-0205-494c-8973-68ae0e9667a8','a3cbc4d7-ad40-4340-a1eb-1deff4d2c93f',replace('We had an outstanding experience.\nThe place is incredibly beautiful and peaceful, the food was fantastic and the service was excellent.\nGretell, Mariela and the rest of the Munay Sonqo team made us feel at home and they took care of every little detail to ensure we had a great time.','\n',char(10)),'Clelia Cayama',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('3d111606-0c0a-47f3-a58a-21c2f088f91e','a3cbc4d7-ad40-4340-a1eb-1deff4d2c93f','Munay Sonqo es un lugar verdaderamente especial, donde la naturaleza te abraza y la montaña te saluda cada día. Desde el primer momento se siente una energía de paz y conexión única. La comida está hecha con amor, y eso se percibe en cada detalle y en cada sabor. Además, Mariela nos brindó un trato muy especial y nos hizo sentir en casa desde el primer instante. La calidez de cada persona que forma parte de este lugar hace que la experiencia sea aún más memorable. Sin duda, es un sitio lleno de alma que queda en el corazón.','Milli Castillo',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('4a7bd43a-0e08-44b7-8196-0759e6e70bb4','783ca547-5c92-43d9-9624-c4436d71e550','Adrian was super helpful!','Brittany Jackson Machmer',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('9b915295-41ac-4b77-b6d6-7d9bf322917e','783ca547-5c92-43d9-9624-c4436d71e550','Excelente','Luis Alberto Camargo Cerron',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('dc289a3d-dfe6-41f6-b8c1-95bdc9c1314c','df692be7-5351-4304-8ff1-ed468d52e0c8','Los más hermoso de estar en SAMDHI es muestra sagrada familia  siempre presente ❤️🫂❤️','Rosa Sallo lozano',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('7848f0c7-afe7-48f0-b87f-5896770187a4','df692be7-5351-4304-8ff1-ed468d52e0c8','This is one of the most beautiful and deep retreat centers in the world. Thank you Fernando and the entire family for the love you share.','Branden Collinsworth',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('241250c2-8f1b-45a7-b7c4-1798da3eec98','df692be7-5351-4304-8ff1-ed468d52e0c8','Very grateful to Fernando and his family for opening up this space to me as a solo traveller before a group retreat. This place is pure magic. It is so tranquil and the majestic view of the mountains from all corners of the property calms you immediately. You can also tell that Fernando and his family has put so much care into this land. Take the time to walk around and you would observe the many plants and flowers they are cultivating. There’s no better place to practise yoga than the amazing shala and I appreciated the practice with Fernando. I also truly appreciate the kindness and smiles from every one here. It is a blessing to be here and i hope more people get to enjoy this paradise on earth. Mucho gracias! 🙏🏼❤️','J',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('c3d7cb50-aee0-40cb-b5dd-cbc5c9c9599c','91362fd3-2fe3-417b-9185-26a1b920c877','I can''t say enough positive things about Jyl and our stay at El Verde. Sacred Valley is a magical place to begin with and Jyl and the space she has created only add to the wonder.  From a feeling of being welcomed to wonderful meals made of local fresh foods to an amazing garden space with mountain views to great accomodations and more, El Verde was a retreat in its truest sense.  Thank you, Jyl for all your hard work to make us feel both welcomed and special!','Marissa Levine',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('9586d5e6-541d-4cea-8a6f-547496f1cee6','91362fd3-2fe3-417b-9185-26a1b920c877',replace('I recently brought a group of women to El Verde Peru, and as a retreat leader who has been guiding retreats for the past six years, I can honestly say this experience was one of the very best.\n\nJyl has thought of every detail and has created a space that feels warm, welcoming, and---well, magical. From each thoughtfully prepared meal to the around-the-clock availability of specialty teas and the cozy nightly fires in the fireplace, we felt deeply cared for every step of the way. The rooms were spotless, yet cleaned daily to maintain a level of cleanliness that is above and beyond anything I have experienced before.\n\nThe gardens are stunning. Each day we discovered something new... a hidden nook, blooming flowers we missed the day before, hummingbirds moving through the space, a surprise around every flower! The land, surrounded by the mountains, feels alive and intentional. Set in a small, rural community, we felt both part of a community but also experienced the quiet needed when on retreat.\n\nThe Sacred Valley is powerful on its own, but what Jyl has created at El Verde truly elevates the experience of being there. There is a sense of care in every corner of the property. It allowed our group to settle in, connect with one another, and fully receive the beauty of Peru... and as a retreat leader, I couldn''t hope for anything more!\n\nI would return in a heartbeat (in fact, I''m looking at just when we might go back right now!).','\n',char(10)),'Jennifer French',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('dbf8a272-a3ad-4870-be6e-a9d44a2e9299','91362fd3-2fe3-417b-9185-26a1b920c877','Just returned from an awsome yoga week at El Verde.  The owner, Jyl, is a kind soul who worked very hard to quietly allow the week to unfold in a peaceful & powerful experience.  The food was fresh, delicious & fun.  My room was cozy, clean & beautiful.  The gardens, framed by the mountains were alive with hummingbirds, bees & beauty.The yoga studio was well equiped & clean. Jyl arranged a life changing sound bath, a visit to cultural sights, an Inca blessing ceremony as well as a chocolate tasting & hike to a beautiful waterfall. I have returned home with a sense of peace & strength. Thank you Jyl','Alex Kramer',5);
INSERT INTO Review VALUES('75026d25-b5a1-45d7-a445-83674dbb57dc','3cbd4cb1-5217-4904-a796-a3fca90ab640','Eliva gave me a great massage','Google Reviewer',5);
